    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><hr><p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">You leverage your ancestors’ authority and name to give weight to your efforts. Whenever you make a Diplomacy, Deception, or Intimidation check, you can invoke your familial line to call for respect or for authority. Such an act grants you a +1 circumstance bonus to your check against your targets, but against those who are even remotely affiliated or aware of your family name, this bonus increases to +2. At a GM’s discretion, this bonus can increase even further depending on the appropriateness of leveraging their name.</span></p>"
